00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:28.800
that they have lost Ed Truck.
埃德·特拉克去世了。

456
00:20:29.480 --> 00:20:32.200
And then Michael's like, well, I have his number somewhere.
迈克尔说，好吧，我这儿应该有他的号码。

457
00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:33.380
I can find it for you.
我可以帮你找找。

458
00:20:33.820 --> 00:20:34.300
Yeah.
是啊。

459
00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:38.060
And she's like, no, Michael, Ed Truck has died.
简说，不，迈克尔，埃德·特拉克已经去世了。

460
00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:39.960
He goes out into the room.
他走到外面的办公室。

461
00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:41.400
He breaks the news to everybody.
他把这个消息告诉了大家。

462
00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:43.520
Kelly rushes up, gives him a hug.
凯莉冲过去，给了他一个拥抱。

463
00:20:43.520 --> 00:20:47.500
Oh, we have a special appearance by Kelly's Extensions and her bangs.
哦，凯莉的接发和刘海特别出镜了。

464
00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:49.060
They make a special appearance.
它们特别出镜了。

465
00:20:49.420 --> 00:20:51.920
They are hugging Michael, giving him some comfort.
它们在拥抱迈克尔，给他一些安慰。

466
00:20:52.240 --> 00:20:55.600
And then Michael approaches Pam for a little awkward hug.
然后迈克尔走向帕姆，进行了一个尴尬的拥抱。

467
00:20:55.760 --> 00:20:56.920
So awkward.
太尴尬了。

468
00:20:57.260 --> 00:20:59.780
And lady, I have a track moment.
女士，我有个追踪时刻。

469
00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:00.800
I'm tracking it.
我正在追踪它。

470
00:21:01.140 --> 00:21:01.540
I'm tracking it.
我正在追踪它。

471
00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:02.040
What are you tracking?
你在追踪什么？

472
00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:06.720
You know, I love to track the plants at front reception.
你知道的，我喜欢追踪前台的植物。

473
00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:08.480
Are there more new plants?
又有新植物了吗？

474
00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:14.220
Well, whatever happens to them, they make an appearance and then we never see them again.
不管它们发生了什么，它们出现一次后我们就再也见不到它们了。

475
00:21:14.720 --> 00:21:18.960
At three minutes, 29 seconds, I am pretty sure that's a succulent.
在三分二十九秒的时候，我敢肯定那是一株多肉植物。

476
00:21:19.600 --> 00:21:20.960
We have a succulent.
我们有一株多肉植物。

477
00:21:22.500 --> 00:21:23.440
Succulent alert.
多肉警报。

478
00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:26.020
Succulent alert at front reception.
前台多肉警报。

479
00:21:26.020 --> 00:21:27.680
We'll probably never see it again.
我们可能再也见不到它了。

480
00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:32.560
But when Michael hugs Pam awkwardly, you get a nice shot of that succulent.
但当迈克尔尴尬地拥抱帕姆时，你正好能拍到那株多肉植物。

481
00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:34.540
I'm not kidding.
我没开玩笑。

482
00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:36.580
I really need to start a spreadsheet.
我真的需要开始做个电子表格了。

483
00:21:36.580 --> 00:21:39.560
I know, a really complex spreadsheet.
我知道，一个非常复杂的电子表格。

484
00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:41.260
All the things we're tracking.
记录我们正在追踪的所有事情。

485
00:21:42.100 --> 00:21:49.160
Well, next we move over to the Stanford office and a staff meeting becomes very awkward when
接下来我们转到斯坦福办公室，一场员工会议变得非常尴尬，因为

486
00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:52.640
Josh is super sexist and condescending to Karen.
乔什对凯伦表现得非常大男子主义且居高临下。

487
00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:55.320
Oh, he was.
哦，确实如此。

488
00:21:55.340 --> 00:21:57.520
He sort of just totally dismissed her.
他简直完全无视了她。

489
00:21:57.880 --> 00:21:58.320
I know.
我知道。

490
00:21:58.940 --> 00:22:00.380
Yeah, seriously.
是啊，说真的。

491
00:22:00.700 --> 00:22:03.640
And then he puts Jim in charge of her for the day.
然后他让吉姆负责她这一天的工作。

492
00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:04.760
Oh, gross.
哦，真恶心。

493
00:22:05.340 --> 00:22:06.100
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

494
00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:13.260
Is this just like, this is like a physical representation of mansplaining, I feel like.
我觉得这简直就是“男式说教”的实体化表现。

495
00:22:13.500 --> 00:22:13.640
Yeah.
是啊。

496
00:22:14.440 --> 00:22:14.900
You know what?
你知道吗？

497
00:22:14.920 --> 00:22:15.500
It's just inaction.
这简直是无所作为。

498
00:22:15.500 --> 00:22:16.720
Jim, why don't you check in on that?
吉姆，你为什么不去跟进一下那个？

499
00:22:17.580 --> 00:22:19.480
Yeah, why don't you oversee that, Jim?
是啊，吉姆，你为什么不负责监督那个？

500
00:22:19.500 --> 00:22:20.660
Why don't you check in on that?
你为什么不去跟进一下那个？

501
00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:23.040
And she's like, yeah, thanks.
然后她说，好的，谢谢。

502
00:22:23.040 --> 00:22:23.600
Yeah, thanks.
好的，谢谢。

503
00:22:23.860 --> 00:22:24.500
Yeah, thanks.
好的，谢谢。

504
00:22:25.120 --> 00:22:27.800
Well, we had a fan catch from Brandon.
嗯，我们收到了一条来自Brandon的粉丝发现。

505
00:22:27.800 --> 00:22:33.580
Brandon, he says, at three minutes and 42 seconds, when Karen is flipping through her stack of
Brandon说，在3分42秒时，当Karen翻看她那一叠

506
00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:37.240
papers, I think I see a page from the script in her note.
文件时，我好像看到了她笔记里夹着一页剧本。

507
00:22:38.700 --> 00:22:40.420
Oh, that's such a good catch.
噢，真是个了不起的发现。

508
00:22:40.760 --> 00:22:41.320
You do.
确实看到了。

509
00:22:42.100 --> 00:22:43.040
I froze it.
我把画面定格了。

510
00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:43.520
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

511
00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:45.640
She's got a little script page.
她确实有一小页剧本。

512
00:22:45.820 --> 00:22:46.760
We used to do that.
我们以前也常那样做。

513
00:22:46.860 --> 00:22:47.600
Remember, Ange?
记得吗，Ange？

514
00:22:47.720 --> 00:22:50.520
We used to hide script pages in our notebooks.
我们以前常把剧本页藏在笔记本里。

515
00:22:50.960 --> 00:22:52.480
I used to keep them in a drawer.
我以前常把它们放在抽屉里。

516
00:22:52.760 --> 00:22:57.100
Like, in between takes, I would open my drawer and I would be like, okay, wait, did I get it?
比如在拍摄间隙，我会打开抽屉，心想，好吧，等等，我记住了吗？

517
00:22:57.160 --> 00:22:57.840
Did I get it to get it?
我真的记住了吗？

518
00:22:57.840 --> 00:22:58.820
And then I shut my drawer again?
然后我又关上抽屉？

519
00:22:59.200 --> 00:22:59.300
Yes.
是的。

520
00:22:59.460 --> 00:23:04.660
We had scripts hidden everywhere on that set that we could just peek at between scenes to
我们在片场到处都藏了剧本，这样在拍摄间隙我们就能偷瞄一眼，

521
00:23:04.660 --> 00:23:08.480
make sure we were, like, on our lines or if we wanted to, like, prep right before.
确保我们没忘词，或者如果想在开拍前再准备一下的话。

522
00:23:08.780 --> 00:23:11.240
I mean, obviously, we had worked on them and we knew our lines.
我是说，显然我们都做过功课，也背下了台词。

523
00:23:11.240 --> 00:23:14.380
But when you're doing a bunch of takes, sometimes you're like, oh, wait, crap, what was that?
但当你拍很多条的时候，有时你会想，噢，等等，糟糕，那句是什么来着？

524
00:23:14.480 --> 00:23:16.320
And you just want to do a quick peek.
你就是想快速瞄一眼。

525
00:23:16.880 --> 00:23:22.620
But also, you know, they would have their writer's draft and then we would read it at a table read
而且，你知道，他们会有编剧初稿，然后我们会在剧本围读会上读它，

526
00:23:22.620 --> 00:23:26.220
and then they would make a bunch of changes and they would start on Monday with what was
接着他们会做很多修改，周一开拍时用的就是

527
00:23:26.220 --> 00:23:27.260
called the shooting draft.
所谓的拍摄定稿。

528
00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:28.380
And that's what I have.
我手里就有那个。

529
00:23:28.500 --> 00:23:30.680
I have a bunch of shooting drafts left over.
我留下了很多拍摄定稿。

530
00:23:30.940 --> 00:23:35.960
But every single morning we would arrive to work and there would be a stack of new pages.
但每天早上我们到片场时，都会有一叠新页面。

531
00:23:36.120 --> 00:23:40.120
They were rewritten scenes just for that day.
那是专门为当天重写的场景。

532
00:23:40.340 --> 00:23:43.200
They would hand you the pages sometimes that morning and be like, okay, here we go, guys.
他们有时会在那天早上把页面发给你，然后说，好了，我们要开始了，伙计们。

533
00:23:43.600 --> 00:23:44.900
These are your changes for the day.
这些是你们今天的改动。

534
00:23:45.260 --> 00:23:49.040
You better believe we were hiding pages in our desks and notebooks.
你最好相信我们当时确实把页面藏在桌子和笔记本里。

535
00:23:49.260 --> 00:23:50.900
But yes, Brandon, you saw one.
但没错，Brandon，你确实发现了一处。

536
00:23:51.200 --> 00:23:54.240
That just tickled me because that is so true.
这让我觉得很有趣，因为这太真实了。

537
00:23:54.440 --> 00:23:55.740
That was a good catch.
那真是个好发现。

538
00:23:55.740 --> 00:24:01.460
Okay, so now at four minutes, two seconds, Karen is really disappointed, you guys, because the chips
好了，现在在4分02秒，Karen真的很失望，伙计们，因为她喜欢的薯片

539
00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:03.340
that she likes, they're not in the vending machine.
不在自动贩卖机里。

540
00:24:03.360 --> 00:24:06.580
But I think Jim felt bad at the way Josh treated her.
但我认为Jim对Josh对待她的方式感到过意不去。

541
00:24:06.720 --> 00:24:08.740
And he now wants to make amends, right?
所以他现在想弥补，对吧？

542
00:24:08.860 --> 00:24:12.040
He wants to try to help her find these potato chips.
他想试着帮她找到这些薯片。

543
00:24:12.040 --> 00:24:20.320
And this whole scene about Karen and her potato chips just got me thinking about Rashida's
关于Karen和她薯片的整个场景让我想到了Rashida的

544
00:24:20.320 --> 00:24:21.240
breakfast order.
早餐订单。

545
00:24:21.820 --> 00:24:22.380
Okay.
好吧。

546
00:24:22.720 --> 00:24:24.840
Do you remember her breakfast order?
你还记得她的早餐订单吗？

547
00:24:25.260 --> 00:24:25.820
No.
不记得。

548
00:24:26.100 --> 00:24:26.380
Okay.
好吧。

549
00:24:26.440 --> 00:24:29.260
Well, we often were in hair and makeup together at the same time.
嗯，我们经常同时在化妆间做造型。

550
00:24:30.120 --> 00:24:36.340
And I texted her because I was like, Rashida, I totally just had this memory of your breakfast
我给她发了短信，因为我想，Rashida，我完全想起了你的早餐

551
00:24:36.340 --> 00:24:36.620
order.
点餐。

552
00:24:36.780 --> 00:24:39.240
Here was the great thing about our caterer, Sergio.
我们的餐饮承办商塞尔吉奥（Sergio）有个很棒的地方。

553
00:24:39.240 --> 00:24:43.840
First of all, he was amazing, but if your order became kind of popular, if other people
首先，他做的饭菜非常棒，但如果你的订单变得很受欢迎，如果其他人

554
00:24:43.840 --> 00:24:46.200
liked it, you would get your name on the menu.
也喜欢的话，你的名字就会出现在菜单上。

555
00:24:46.680 --> 00:24:47.120
Yes.
没错。

556
00:24:47.240 --> 00:24:52.340
So you would walk up to the truck to order breakfast in the morning, the food truck, and you could
所以你早上走到餐车去点早餐时，那个餐车，你可以

557
00:24:52.340 --> 00:24:54.960
order a Rashida Angela size.
点一份“拉什达·安吉拉”份量的餐点。

558
00:24:55.500 --> 00:24:59.840
Because I always wanted everything half portion because it was just big.
因为我总是想要半份，因为分量实在太大了。

559
00:25:00.100 --> 00:25:01.900
The portions were big and I'm a little person.
分量很大，而我个子比较小。

560
00:25:01.900 --> 00:25:03.780
So I'd always say, can I have half of that?
所以我总是说，能给我半份吗？

561
00:25:03.780 --> 00:25:05.740
So they started calling it Angela size.
于是他们开始把它叫作“安吉拉”份量。

562
00:25:06.040 --> 00:25:07.980
So here's what the Rashida was.
这就是“拉什达”套餐的内容。

563
00:25:08.160 --> 00:25:13.480
And Sergio, I ran into Sergio a while back because I was working on a Netflix show and
而且塞尔吉奥，我前阵子碰到了塞尔吉奥，因为我当时在拍一部网飞的剧，

564
00:25:13.480 --> 00:25:16.500
he was the caterer for it for Mindy's show, Never Have I Ever.
他是明迪（Mindy）那部剧《好想做一次》的餐饮承办商。

565
00:25:16.760 --> 00:25:17.680
He was the caterer.
他就是那个承办商。

566
00:25:17.960 --> 00:25:18.080
Yeah.
对。

567
00:25:18.280 --> 00:25:20.240
Mindy hired him, which was fantastic.
明迪雇了他，这真是太棒了。

568
00:25:20.500 --> 00:25:21.960
We had a little mini office reunion.
我们举行了一次小型的《办公室》重聚。

569
00:25:23.360 --> 00:25:26.860
And here's the Rashida, which you can still order from Sergio.
这就是“拉什达”套餐，你现在依然可以从塞尔吉奥那里点到。

570
00:25:27.120 --> 00:25:27.260
Ready?
准备好了吗？

571
00:25:27.700 --> 00:25:28.100
Yes.
好了。

572
00:25:28.440 --> 00:25:33.960
A corn tortilla, poached egg, black beans, avocado, turkey bacon, cholula on the side.
玉米饼、水煮蛋、黑豆、牛油果、火鸡培根，旁边配上乔卢拉辣酱。

573
00:25:36.500 --> 00:25:38.460
And I was texting with Rashida about it.
我当时正和拉什达发短信聊这个。

574
00:25:38.500 --> 00:25:41.020
She was like, I don't even know how I functioned after eating that.
她说，我甚至不知道吃完那个之后我是怎么正常工作的。

575
00:25:41.200 --> 00:25:43.600
Like, why should I have just gone and taken a nap?
就像是，我为什么不直接去睡一觉呢？

576
00:25:43.780 --> 00:25:45.420
But that's called the Rashida.
但那个就叫“拉什达”套餐。

577
00:25:46.000 --> 00:25:48.780
But I can get that Angela size if I'm not that hungry.
如果我没那么饿，我还可以点“安吉拉”份量的。

578
00:25:48.920 --> 00:25:50.660
Yeah, I'd like the Rashida Angela size, please.
好的，请给我来一份“拉什达·安吉拉”份量的。

579
00:25:51.040 --> 00:25:53.200
Oh my gosh, that brought back so many memories.
天哪，这勾起了我好多回忆。

580
00:25:54.200 --> 00:26:01.040
Molly Neck wrote in to say, guys, you can see her favorite chips in the vending machine slot B1.
莫莉·内克（Molly Neck）来信说，伙计们，你们可以在自动贩卖机的B1槽位看到她最喜欢的薯片。

581
00:26:01.220 --> 00:26:08.620
Okay, so there's a row of potato chips in the vending machine, but apparently those aren't the ones that Karen wants.
好的，自动贩卖机里有一排薯片，但显然那些不是凯伦（Karen）想要的。

582
00:26:08.780 --> 00:26:11.100
Yes, Karen wants salt and vinegar potato chips.
没错，凯伦想要的是盐醋味薯片。

583
00:26:11.280 --> 00:26:13.980
I did a mini deep dive on hers potato chips.
我专门对赫尔斯（Herr's）薯片做了一番小小的深度调查。

584
00:26:14.300 --> 00:26:18.900
And Philadelphia Magazine did a ranking of all the hers potato chips.
《费城杂志》对所有的赫尔斯薯片做了一个排名。

585
00:26:19.080 --> 00:26:21.320
And salt and vinegar was their number one chip.
而盐醋味是他们的第一名。

586
00:26:22.180 --> 00:26:26.960
So it might make sense that it was hard to find because it's their, it's the number one chip.
所以它很难找也说得通，因为它是他们的第一名。

587
00:26:27.620 --> 00:26:29.820
Close behind was cheddar horseradish.
紧随其后的是切达辣根味。

588
00:26:30.500 --> 00:26:33.180
Pam's favorite sour cream and onion was number four.
帕姆（Pam）最喜欢的酸奶油洋葱味排在第四。

589
00:26:33.740 --> 00:26:35.820
Our favorite is their barbecue chips.
我们最喜欢的是他们的烧烤味薯片。

590
00:26:36.060 --> 00:26:37.780
I love their hers barbecue chips.
我超爱他们的赫尔斯烧烤味薯片。

591
00:26:37.980 --> 00:26:39.840
I don't know where that is in the ranking.
我不知道那个在排名里排第几。

592
00:26:40.560 --> 00:26:40.740
Okay.
好吧。

593
00:26:40.880 --> 00:26:41.340
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

594
00:26:41.480 --> 00:26:42.420
I didn't look that one up.
我没查那个。

595
00:26:42.560 --> 00:26:42.920
Okay.
好吧。

596
00:26:43.440 --> 00:26:46.400
But I do have a script catch for you as well.
但我这里也有一个剧本里的发现要告诉你。

597
00:26:46.620 --> 00:26:48.420
We're not done talking about this yet.
我们还没聊完这个呢。

598
