所以我知道这一点。

1694
01:13:13.760 --> 01:13:16.560
But I didn't know you were a walking one-man show.
但我不知道你还是个行走的单人秀。

1695
01:13:16.860 --> 01:13:19.320
Suffice it to say, Rain knew his stuff.
总之，雷恩确实很有料。

1696
01:13:20.000 --> 01:13:24.400
And we did rehearse, but just a little bit right before the scene.
我们确实排练过，但就在拍戏前稍微练了一下。

1697
01:13:24.620 --> 01:13:26.200
Rain and I practiced separately.
雷恩和我分开练习的。

1698
01:13:26.460 --> 01:13:29.520
I had listened to the song over and over again to memorize the words.
我把那首歌听了一遍又一遍，为了记住歌词。

1699
01:13:29.720 --> 01:13:33.180
I had to sing the first verse through the chorus.
我必须从第一段唱到副歌。

1700
01:13:33.940 --> 01:13:35.860
That's what I had to do over and over again.
那就是我一遍又一遍必须做的事情。

1701
01:13:36.500 --> 01:13:37.920
I was so nervous.
我当时紧张极了。

1702
01:13:38.420 --> 01:13:40.120
Well, I thought you did fantastic.
噢，我觉得你表现得棒极了。

1703
01:13:41.260 --> 01:13:42.020
Thank you.
谢谢。

1704
01:13:42.240 --> 01:13:44.420
I have a fan question from the scene, Jenna.
珍娜，我这儿有个粉丝关于那个场景的问题。

1705
01:13:45.220 --> 01:13:45.480
Okay.
好的。

1706
01:13:46.180 --> 01:13:51.240
So Chelsea wrote in and said, was Angela's A-man improvised?
切尔西来信问，安吉拉那句“阿门”是即兴发挥的吗？

1707
01:13:51.420 --> 01:13:55.840
A lot of people wrote in about this because it was so quick after Pam was done talking.
很多人都写信问过这个问题，因为那句台词在帕姆说完话后接得太快了。

1708
01:13:55.980 --> 01:13:57.900
People wanted to know if I improvised that.
大家都想知道那是不是我即兴说的。

1709
01:13:58.080 --> 01:13:59.640
No, that was scripted.
不，那是剧本里写好的。

1710
01:13:59.640 --> 01:14:03.280
And folks wanted to know why did Angela do it.
大家还想知道安吉拉为什么要那么做。

1711
01:14:03.400 --> 01:14:13.900
And I said, I think personally, the direction that, you know, they gave me was that Angela had had enough of this charade, this bird funeral.
我个人觉得，导演给我的指导是，安吉拉已经受够了这场闹剧，这场鸟的葬礼。

1712
01:14:14.100 --> 01:14:15.480
Pam had gone on and on.
帕姆没完没了地说个不停。

1713
01:14:15.600 --> 01:14:15.860
Enough.
够了。

1714
01:14:16.000 --> 01:14:16.240
Amen.
阿门。

1715
01:14:16.480 --> 01:14:17.160
I'm done.
我受够了。

1716
01:14:17.580 --> 01:14:18.360
And that...
而那……

1717
01:14:18.360 --> 01:14:19.720
That's how you finish it.
那就是你结束这一切的方式。

1718
01:14:19.820 --> 01:14:20.180
Yes.
没错。

1719
01:14:20.460 --> 01:14:20.700
Amen.
阿门。

1720
01:14:21.200 --> 01:14:21.600
I'm finished.
我说完了。

1721
01:14:21.820 --> 01:14:21.960
Amen.
阿门。

1722
01:14:22.200 --> 01:14:22.720
Stop talking.
别再说了。

1723
01:14:23.460 --> 01:14:24.460
Yes, exactly.
对，就是这样。

1724
01:14:25.380 --> 01:14:27.460
Speaking of the script, I have a script catch.
说到剧本，我发现了一个剧本上的出入。

1725
01:14:27.660 --> 01:14:27.800
Okay.
好的。

1726
01:14:27.800 --> 01:14:30.140
So, you know, in the scene, we set the box on fire.
你知道，在那个场景里，我们把盒子点着了。

1727
01:14:30.400 --> 01:14:33.360
In the shooting draft of the script, we buried the bird.
但在拍摄用的剧本草稿里，我们是把鸟埋了。

1728
01:14:34.060 --> 01:14:39.820
There was a scene where Michael and Dwight are digging a hole outside, and then we all gather around this hole.
原本有一场戏是迈克尔和德怀特在外面挖坑，然后我们所有人都聚在坑边。

1729
01:14:40.300 --> 01:14:43.160
And it got changed to fire, but I don't know why.
后来改成了火葬，但我不知道为什么。

1730
01:14:43.160 --> 01:14:49.620
I think maybe, Angela, there was really no grass in this area that we shot.
我想可能是因为，安吉拉，我们拍摄的那块地方根本没有草坪。

1731
01:14:49.620 --> 01:14:50.480
We had no grass.
我们那儿没草。

1732
01:14:50.680 --> 01:14:55.580
There was a hedge with maybe, like, I don't know, three feet of dirt.
只有一道树篱，后面大概只有三英尺宽的泥地。

1733
01:14:56.000 --> 01:14:57.780
Like, yeah, there was, I mean...
是啊，我是说……

1734
01:14:57.800 --> 01:14:58.380
Not even.
甚至还不到。

1735
01:14:58.600 --> 01:15:06.080
There is a deleted scene where Michael and Dwight are trying to dig a hole there, and then the business on the other side yells at them, and they run away.
有一个删减片段是迈克尔和德怀特试图在那儿挖坑，然后对面的人冲他们大喊大叫，他们就跑了。

1736
01:15:06.820 --> 01:15:07.320
Oh!
噢！

1737
01:15:07.700 --> 01:15:08.160
Okay.
好吧。

1738
01:15:08.480 --> 01:15:09.380
Well, there you go.
原来如此。

1739
01:15:09.880 --> 01:15:13.140
Well, we had another fan question about this fire, then.
那我们还有另一个关于这场火的粉丝提问。

1740
01:15:13.480 --> 01:15:17.360
Clara Johnson wants to know, did you actually set the bird on fire?
克拉拉·约翰逊想知道，你们真的把那只鸟点着了吗？

1741
01:15:18.180 --> 01:15:18.680
Yes.
是的。

1742
01:15:18.900 --> 01:15:20.480
Real fire, fake bird.
真火，假鸟。

1743
01:15:20.700 --> 01:15:27.740
Kent told me they had to hire a special effects guy to oversee the fire and the extinguishing, and they had to get a special permit.
肯特告诉我，他们必须雇一个特效人员来监督点火和灭火过程，而且还得申请特别许可证。

1744
01:15:27.800 --> 01:15:29.300
To be allowed to set the fire.
才能获准点火。

1745
01:15:29.700 --> 01:15:31.600
And he said we did three takes.
他说我们拍了三次。

1746
01:15:32.180 --> 01:15:33.420
Three takes of the fire.
火烧了三次。

1747
01:15:33.720 --> 01:15:41.740
And Phil told me, though, that the special effects guys were worried that the fake dead bird might give off toxic fumes when it burned.
不过菲尔告诉我，特效人员担心那只假死鸟燃烧时会产生有毒烟雾。

1748
01:15:41.740 --> 01:15:46.380
So we, they actually took it out of the box and just put a wad of toilet paper in there.
所以他们实际上把它从盒子里拿了出来，只在里面放了一团卫生纸。

1749
01:15:46.720 --> 01:15:48.700
Oh, not toilet paper.
噢，不是卫生纸吧。

1750
01:15:49.580 --> 01:15:50.500
I know.
我知道。

1751
01:15:51.060 --> 01:15:51.760
Too soon.
太早了。

1752
01:15:51.760 --> 01:15:51.900
I know.
我知道。

1753
01:15:52.100 --> 01:15:52.960
Too soon, Angela.
太早了，安吉拉。

1754
01:15:53.260 --> 01:15:53.720
Too soon.
太早了。

1755
01:15:55.200 --> 01:15:59.720
And then, finally, we had a fan catch from Peter K.
最后，我们收到了彼得·K发来的粉丝留言。

1756
01:16:00.040 --> 01:16:03.740
He said, I noticed the box was burned in some shredded paper.
他说，我注意到盒子里烧了一些碎纸。

1757
01:16:04.280 --> 01:16:07.620
Could this be further evidence that Pam does use the shredder?
这是否能进一步证明帕姆确实用了碎纸机？

1758
01:16:07.620 --> 01:16:09.740
Oh, look at that.
噢，快看那个。

1759
01:16:10.180 --> 01:16:11.160
Nice one, Peter.
干得好，彼得。

1760
01:16:11.640 --> 01:16:12.640
It would appear so.
看起来确实如此。

1761
01:16:13.080 --> 01:16:17.620
Well, you know, Jen actually left us a really great message about this scene.
嗯，你知道，简实际上给我们留了一条关于这一幕的非常棒的留言。

1762
01:16:18.040 --> 01:16:22.960
And she was talking about the fact that we never got to shoot outside.
她谈到了我们从未在户外拍摄过这一点。

1763
01:16:22.960 --> 01:16:25.940
And when we did, everyone would get really excited.
而当我们真的去户外时，每个人都会感到非常兴奋。

1764
01:16:26.280 --> 01:16:28.580
And she explains a little bit about that.
她对此做了一些解释。

1765
01:16:28.780 --> 01:16:30.200
So, Sam, can you play that?
所以，萨姆，你能播放一下吗？

1766
01:16:30.200 --> 01:16:39.220
One thing that I remember from the grief counseling episode is that when I went to the sound mix, they were showing us the playback of the episode.
关于《悲伤辅导》那一集，我记得的一件事是，当我参加混音时，他们正在给我们播放这一集的录像。

1767
01:16:39.720 --> 01:16:43.040
And it was still a little bit unusual when the characters went outside.
当角色们走到户外时，感觉还是有点不寻常。

1768
01:16:43.040 --> 01:16:44.720
It was still a little bit of a treat.
那仍然算是一种难得的体验。

1769
01:16:44.980 --> 01:16:52.020
So we get to this bird funeral scene and our characters are outside.
所以我们拍到了这场鸟儿葬礼的戏，我们的角色都在户外。

1770
01:16:52.220 --> 01:16:58.420
And I just remember hearing kind of an enormous amount of birds.
我只记得当时听到了巨大的鸟叫声。

1771
01:16:58.420 --> 01:17:02.800
And I think that it was because we were outside.
我想那是因为我们在户外。

1772
01:17:02.800 --> 01:17:04.860
It was because we had a bird funeral.
那是因为我们在举行鸟儿葬礼。

1773
01:17:05.820 --> 01:17:14.660
It was so exciting for the amazing sound people, who do a fantastic job, to put a lot of bird noises in.
对于那些出色的音效师来说，能加入大量的鸟叫声一定非常令人兴奋，他们做得太棒了。

1774
01:17:14.760 --> 01:17:25.740
Because for the longest time, when we're inside the office, they're just putting dot matrix printer sounds and just faxes and old-fashioned office noises.
因为在很长一段时间里，当我们待在办公室里时，他们只能加入针式打印机的声音，还有传真机和老式办公室的噪音。

1775
01:17:25.740 --> 01:17:34.280
So it must have been such a treat and a field day to be able to go outside and hear birds, and especially on theme with the funeral.
所以能去户外听到鸟叫声，尤其是还契合葬礼的主题，对他们来说一定是一种享受，也是一次大显身手的机会。

1776
01:17:34.600 --> 01:17:45.060
So I remember, it was a slight exaggeration, but it sounded a little bit like Alfred Hitchcock, the birds, when I first heard the playback for the bird funeral.
所以我记得，虽然有点夸张，但当我第一次听到鸟儿葬礼的录音回放时，那些鸟叫声听起来有点像阿尔弗雷德·希区柯克的电影。

1777
01:17:45.060 --> 01:17:51.040
But they quickly made a wonderful adjustment, and it was the right amount of outside birds.
但他们很快做出了极好的调整，户外鸟叫声的量恰到好处。

1778
01:17:52.300 --> 01:17:53.340
I love that.
我喜欢这一点。

1779
01:17:53.460 --> 01:17:55.680
I love that our sound mixers got so excited.
我喜欢我们的混音师们如此兴奋的样子。

1780
01:17:55.840 --> 01:18:00.780
They put like hundreds of birds, and they were like, okay, guys, there's not this many birds outside.
他们加了成百上千只鸟，然后他们意识到，好吧，伙计们，外面没这么多鸟。

1781
01:18:01.100 --> 01:18:02.740
Let's dial it back.
我们调小一点吧。

1782
01:18:03.700 --> 01:18:04.880
Yes, yes.
是的，是的。

1783
01:18:05.380 --> 01:18:08.820
Oh, what good insight from Jen this week.
噢，简这周的见解真好。

1784
01:18:08.820 --> 01:18:14.000
Yes, thank you so much, Jen Salata, for sending in those clips and for texting me.
是的，非常感谢简·萨拉塔发来这些片段并给我发短信。

1785
01:18:14.240 --> 01:18:15.260
You are amazing.
你太棒了。

1786
01:18:15.260 --> 01:18:16.480
We so appreciate it.
我们非常感激。

1787
01:18:16.600 --> 01:18:22.060
And thank you, Rashida, for letting me bug you about all kinds of random things yesterday.
也谢谢你，拉什达，昨天让我为了各种琐事烦扰你。

1788
01:18:22.340 --> 01:18:27.980
And also, Phil Shea and Kent Sabornak, thank you guys for helping us make this podcast so great.
还有，菲尔·谢伊和肯特·萨博纳克，谢谢你们帮助我们让这个播客变得如此出色。

1789
01:18:28.220 --> 01:18:31.640
And thanks so much to Mindy Kaling for letting us take a clip from your book,
也非常感谢敏迪·卡灵允许我们引用你书中的片段，

1790
01:18:31.920 --> 01:18:34.520
Is Everyone Hanging Out Without Me and Other Concerns.
《大家都背着我出去玩吗？及其他忧虑》。

1791
01:18:34.540 --> 01:18:35.240
It's hilarious.
那本书太搞笑了。

1792
01:18:35.560 --> 01:18:36.280
We love you, Mindy.
我们爱你，敏迪。

1793
01:18:36.840 --> 01:18:38.260
So there you have it, guys.
好了，伙计们，就是这样。

1794
01:18:38.260 --> 01:18:40.300
That's the grief counseling episode.
这就是《悲伤辅导》那一集。

1795
01:18:40.640 --> 01:18:41.680
Did we do it?
我们做到了吗？

1796
01:18:41.840 --> 01:18:43.200
Are we leaving you depressed?
我们没让你们感到沮丧吧？

1797
01:18:43.200 --> 01:18:44.060
I hope not.
希望没有。

1798
01:18:44.160 --> 01:18:44.860
I hope not.
希望没有。

1799
01:18:45.020 --> 01:18:49.860
And hopefully next week, we won't have any more dead birds to tell you about in our lives.
希望下周我们的生活中不会再有死鸟要告诉你们了。

1800
01:18:50.000 --> 01:18:51.960
Stay safe out there, flying friends.
在外出时注意安全，飞翔的朋友们。

1801
01:18:52.120 --> 01:18:53.680
Stay safe out there, everyone.
大家在外注意安全。

1802
01:18:53.880 --> 01:18:54.340
We love you.
我们爱你们。

1803
01:18:57.800 --> 01:18:59.720
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

